  "id": "noise-effects",
  "term": "noise effects",
  "definition": "In cognitive psychology, noise effects are changes in performance caused by noise, especially in complex activities such as reading, writing, or calculation. The source emphasizes that to understand these effects in real settings like schools or offices, researchers should study the complex task itself rather than relying only on simpler underlying abilities such as working memory.",
